# Everything this repository ships is tracked. Two things deliberately are not.
#
# 1. _work/ — the scratch and private side of the project: source captures kept for
#    provenance, the running worklog, the pre-publication fact check, reviewer notes.
#    These used to sit in notes/ beside the shipped methods notes, one entry in this file
#    each, so nothing about the folder told you which kind a file was.
#
#    It now also holds the manuscript sources and the assembler that builds paper/draft.md
#    from them, which makes this line a real decision and not housekeeping: the tracked
#    deliverable is the assembled paper/draft.md, and a clone cannot re-run the assembly.
#    The reason it stays out is that the assembler works by lifting line ranges out of the
#    pre-reframe draft, so shipping it would ship superseded claims alongside the paper.
#    Everything a replication needs — the data, the code that produces every number, and
#    the tests that pin them — is tracked. What is not tracked is how the prose was laid
#    out. If that trade stops being worth it, the fix is to inline the remaining lifts into
#    _work/manuscript/ and track that folder, not to track the pre-reframe draft.
# 2. Regenerated output: caches, bytecode, and the LaTeX intermediates build_pdf.py
#    writes on its way to the PDF.
#
# So notes/ now holds exactly what someone cloning this repository gets.

_work/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.DS_Store
*.tmp
*.bak
*.zip

# PDF build intermediates (regenerated by src/build_pdf.py)
paper/_build.md
paper/_header.tex
paper/_pg/
paper/_pgcheck/
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log

# Coverage data (measured on demand, never shipped)
.coverage
.coverage.*
